    "title": "Write a practical message",
    "subtitle": "A tradeoff in the budget · 1 · preparation 1",
    "context": "Use this subset of the economy vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U5-32. Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare costs, benefits and constraints before making a practical decision.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-32-P01-compose-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Compose a purposeful message",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U5-32-P01-compose-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "written",
            "prompt": "A tradeoff in the budget · 1 · preparation 1: Write a structured recommendation for an absent decision-maker. Explain the issue, compare a plausible alternative, and support your conclusion with specific source evidence and a limitation.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "朋友做一种手工产品，最近订产品的人增加了，产量比以前多。他很高兴，觉得只要卖出的数量增加，留下的钱就一定会更多。\n\n到了月底，他发现留下的钱并没有想的那么多。为了按时交货，他买了价格更高的材料，还请人来帮忙。产品做得多，成本也增加了。\n\n我们把这段时间的情况写下来，不急着判断生意好坏。卖得更多是一件事，做每一件花多少又是另一件事，两者都需要了解。\n\n朋友先联系原来的商家，询问能不能提前订材料，减少临时购买的花费。他没有马上减少产品需要的材料，因为那样可能影响品质。\n\n下一次安排生产时，他把交货时间也考虑进去，不再为了卖给更多人就随便答应。数量少一点，却能按计划完成，也更容易看清楚成本。\n\n朋友说，产量增加并不等于赚的钱一定增加，还要看每件产品花了多少钱。这次以后，他开始认真了解生产的每一步，不再只看卖出了多少件。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Write your own message",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed writing practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "The issue, evidence and conclusion form a coherent argument."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I treated the alternative fairly and retained a limitation on my conclusion."
              }
            ],
            "minLength": 1
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
